            <ArticleTitle>The use of ondansetron to treat pruritus associated with intrathecal morphine in two paediatric patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>337-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intrathecal morphine is an effective technique for providing postoperative analgesia after major surgical procedures in children. Pruritus is a common side effect associated with intrathecal morphine. We report two patients who experienced significant pruritus associated with intrathecal morphine administration and were successfully treated with ondansetron. Ondansetron appears to be a beneficial and safe method of relieving pruritus associated with intrathecal morphine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
